1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,514
An AI agent with your company card.

2
00:00:02,564 --> 00:00:04,125
Who keeps its logbook?

3
00:00:04,175 --> 00:00:08,374
This is Tacho: a tachograph for AI agents, built on Arkiv.

4
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:13,163
Trucks carry tachographs because hauliers once kept their own logbooks.

5
00:00:13,213 --> 00:00:15,164
AI agents are still in that era.

6
00:00:15,214 --> 00:00:20,290
The limits an agent had, and the log of what it did, sit in the vendor's database.

7
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:23,166
The vendor can edit it, lose it, or shut down.

8
00:00:23,216 --> 00:00:26,292
And the fuel station cannot check anything at all.

9
00:00:26,692 --> 00:00:30,083
Here is the whole story, live on the Tiramisu testnet.

10
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:37,283
The fleet owner issues a mandate: fuel and tolls only, fifteen thousand roubles per action, forty thousand a day.

11
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:42,445
It is read-only, and it lives fifteen minutes unless the owner keeps renewing it.

12
00:00:42,495 --> 00:00:52,130
Every attempt the agent makes, allowed or refused, becomes a record from the agent's wallet, handed in the same atomic batch to an address nobody holds.

13
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:55,635
So nobody can delete it, not even the agent's operator.

14
00:00:55,685 --> 00:01:04,173
Three attempts are refused: one over the per-action cap, one for a kind the mandate never granted, one that would break the daily cap.

15
00:01:04,223 --> 00:01:09,144
The fuel station verifies a record before it pumps, and seals its own receipt.

16
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:13,859
A forger copies every attribute into a fake ninety-thousand-rouble record.

17
00:01:13,909 --> 00:01:15,324
Refused: wrong creator.

18
00:01:15,374 --> 00:01:16,790
Then the owner revokes.

19
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:23,162
The agent hears the deletion over a WebSocket, halts, and its next attempt is refused on the record.

20
00:01:23,562 --> 00:01:26,098
Anyone can audit this from Arkiv alone.

21
00:01:26,148 --> 00:01:30,010
The inspector is a static page with no server and no login.

22
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:32,066
The ring counts down the lease.

23
00:01:32,116 --> 00:01:38,962
The disc is the day, like a paper tachograph: green allowed, amber refused, red forged, blue heartbeats.

24
00:01:39,012 --> 00:01:44,797
Every record is sealed, kept forty-five days, and anyone can extend it during a dispute.

25
00:01:44,847 --> 00:01:50,101
Details are encrypted; with the key in the link, only the parties can read them.

26
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:54,544
Each panel shows its exact query, and a curl that works without us.

27
00:01:54,944 --> 00:01:58,247
The fuel station's check trusts nothing the agent says.

28
00:01:58,297 --> 00:02:06,232
It reads the creator field, the mandate as it was at the record's block, and recomputes the daily cap from the agent's own records.

29
00:02:06,282 --> 00:02:07,695
A genuine record passes.

30
00:02:07,745 --> 00:02:11,718
The forged one fails on authorship, whatever attributes it copies.

31
00:02:12,118 --> 00:02:14,528
Take Arkiv away and this falls apart.

32
00:02:14,578 --> 00:02:17,918
Expiry is enforced by the database, not a cron job.

33
00:02:17,968 --> 00:02:20,245
The creator is set by the protocol.

34
00:02:20,295 --> 00:02:22,971
Ownership makes the evidence undeletable.

35
00:02:23,021 --> 00:02:26,228
And a stranger can query all of it, at any block.

36
00:02:26,628 --> 00:02:33,094
Security, censorship resistance, privacy, and an open data contract anyone can build on.

37
00:02:33,144 --> 00:02:37,018
Tacho: leased authority, sealed records, open audits.
